==English==

===Etymology===
As if {{m|en|smack|smacked|hit}} in the {{m|en|gob||mouth (Irish / Scottish gaelic)}}.

Attested since 1959, from Northern English dialect, particularly Liverpool, popularized via television.<ref>[http://www.worldwidewords.org/qa/qa-gob1.htm World Wide Words: Gobsmacked]</ref>

Since 1998, Gobsmacked LTD announced its charge of £1 for every time the word was used outside of its headquarters. This led to the drastic decrease in the using of the word throughout 1998 - 2010. The charge now stands at £0.97 for each use of the word. 

In 2004, 2 men were charged with fines of over £1000 after reportedly using the word illegally on several occasions, without reporting its use to 'GOBSMACKED LTD'.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈɡɒb.smækt/|lang=en}}

